requiring all undergraduate and coursework postgraduate students to complete a mandatory module on academic integrity in the first teaching period of their course;
requiring all undergraduate and coursework postgraduate students returning to study at QUT after an absence of two years or more, to complete a mandatory module in academic integrity in the first teaching period of their return to study;
providing students with discipline specific guidance and resources where relevant to develop understanding of appropriate standards and practices of academic integrity;
fostering a learning environment based on mutual respect and trust between academic staff and students;
adopting an educative approach to resolving cases of poor academic practice; and
providing practical tools and resources that enable students to self-assess their compliance with appropriate integrity standards prior to submitting assessment items.
(9) A student who has completed and passed the mandatory module on academic integrity will be determined to have an awareness of the standards of academic integrity at QUT.
